5e:["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-16 grid grid-cols-1 gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_280px] lg:gap-16","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"min-w-0 space-y-12","children":[["$","$L3",null,{"children":["$","section",null,{"className":"border-t border-border pt-8 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"label-mono flex items-center gap-3 text-muted-foreground","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent-blue","children":"01"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"h-px w-6 bg-border"}],"Overview"]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-5","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground","children":[["$","p","0",{"children":"Alchemist is a backend-oriented bot that watches markets and reports structure. Built in Python around Telegram for delivery, it processes price data through technical concepts — break of structure (BOS), change of character (CHOCH), liquidity levels, fair value gaps (FVG) and market regimes — and turns what it observes into readable, source-cited messages."}],["$","p","1",{"children":"It is an analysis assistant with strict boundaries: it describes what the market did and where structure sits. It does not predict, promise, or advise — and its messages are worded so that stays true even under pressure."}]]}]}]]}]}],["$","$L3",null,{"children":["$","section",null,{"className":"border-t border-border pt-8 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"label-mono flex items-center gap-3 text-muted-foreground","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent-blue","children":"02"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"h-px w-6 bg-border"}],"The problem"]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-5","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground","children":"Market-structure analysis is repetitive and mechanical — exactly the work software should absorb. A human analyst scanning pairs for BOS/CHOCH events, liquidity pools and unmitigated gaps is doing pattern detection at machine speed poorly. The problem is automating the observation while leaving every ounce of the judgement with the human."}]}]]}]}],["$","$L3",null,{"children":["$","section",null,{"className":"border-t border-border pt-8 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"label-mono flex items-center gap-3 text-muted-foreground","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent-blue","children":"03"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"h-px w-6 bg-border"}],"Intended users"]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-5","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground","children":"One primary user: me. Alchemist is a personal research tool that surfaces structure across pairs so my own analysis starts informed instead of starting from a blank chart."}]}]]}]}],["$","$L3",null,{"children":["$","section",null,{"className":"border-t border-border pt-8 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"label-mono flex items-center gap-3 text-muted-foreground","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent-blue","children":"04"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"h-px w-6 bg-border"}],"Key features"]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-5","children":["$","ul",null,{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex gap-4 text-[15px] leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-1.5 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-wider text-accent-blue","children":"01"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-muted-foreground","children":"Structure event detection — BOS and CHOCH"}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"flex gap-4 text-[15px] leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-1.5 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-wider text-accent-blue","children":"02"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-muted-foreground","childr